Provisional family context (member figures — **not** scores for this slug, and each member has its own folder and its own findings files):

- Qwen3.7-Max — 1M context, API-only, ~¥12/¥36 per 1M tokens; the Qwen3.8 blog credits it as the previous flagship generation and reports a 152% improvement over it in the successor's coding/cowork benchmarks.
- Qwen3.7-Plus — 397B total / 17B activated MoE, 1M context, text+image in, $0.32/$1.28 per 1M on OpenRouter; Qwen's own Qwen3.8-Flash-Next card compares against it as the balanced baseline.
- Qwen3.7-Flash — native vision-language tier released 2026-07-15, 1M context, API-only.
- Reddit/LocalLLaMA discussion of Qwen3.7 (open weights expected but never shipped) and a "Qwen3.7 Max Is API-Only" write-up both confirm the generation has no downloadable checkpoint.

### Independent-source comparison and identity resolution

- Alibaba's own Qwen blog covers the generation under the member name: "Qwen3.7: The Agent Frontier" (2026-05-19) is explicitly about **Qwen3.7-Max** ("What sets Qwen3.7-Max apart is the breadth and depth of its agent capabilities") — the generation never appears as a standalone model ([Qwen blog](https://qwen.ai/blog?id=qwen3.7)).
- Alibaba Cloud Model Studio's supported-models overview lists the Qwen3.7 entries as `qwen3.7-plus` (balanced performance, speed and cost — also listed for visual understanding) and `qwen3.7-max`, with `qwen3.7-flash` and `qwen3.7-text-embedding` elsewhere on the same page; no bare `qwen3.7` text SKU ([Model Studio models](https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/model-studio/models), [DashScope API reference](https://help.aliyun.com/zh/model-studio/api-reference)).
- Live independent catalogues agree: OpenRouter's model API exposes only `qwen3.7-flash`, `qwen3.7-max`, `qwen3.7-plus` and `qwen3.7-plus:batch` ([OpenRouter models API](https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models)); models.dev carries the same three members across the `alibaba`, `bailian`, `cline-pass` and `novita` providers and no bare entry ([models.dev API](https://models.dev/api.json)); OpenCode Zen's live catalogue has no Qwen3.7 route at all ([OpenCode Zen models](https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models)).
- No open-weights Qwen3.7 exists: the Hugging Face Qwen organisation model API returns `[]` for the search term `Qwen3.7` on 2026-10-31, and independent write-ups state plainly that Qwen3.7 Max is API-only with no open weights ([HF Qwen org API](https://huggingface.co/api/models?author=Qwen&search=Qwen3.7), [Spheron — Qwen3.7 Max is API-only](https://www.spheron.network/blog/deploy-qwen3-7-max-gpu-cloud/)). Qwen instead shipped open weights for Qwen3.8-27B, whose card compares itself against Qwen3.7-Plus.
- This is the same identity class as two entries already parked in this project: `qwen-3.5` ("generation name, never a model — members tracked as qwen-3.5-397b / qwen-3.5-plus / qwen-3.5-9b") and `gemini-2.5` ("family shorthand for gemini-2.5-pro"). The roster `model-aliases.generated.md` does not yet list `qwen-3.7`, but the rule it encodes applies: a generation name is not a model, and research belongs in the member folder for the ID actually cited.
- Because no exact model exists, no member measurement was merged into this record and no normalized score is defensible. **Recommendation:** park `qwen-3.7` as a generation name and keep the evidence in `model/qwen-3.7-max/`, `model/qwen-3.7-plus/` and `model/qwen-3.7-flash/`. This folder already carries 12 peer findings files (current average 82.3), so the parking decision is a dataset-level change that needs explicit user sign-off — it was not applied here.

